    {
      "id": "2pRYTJiQjjEVor60dQjAS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 992.4049715314572,
      "y": 10195.710597507528,
      "width": 304.4197998046875,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 415387882,
      "version": 182,
      "versionNonce": 1786449974,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1782922853033,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) How data load in Redis\n2) How data load in ES.\n3) What happen if master down\n4) Celebrity problem.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) How data load in Redis\n2) How data load in ES.\n3) What happen if master down\n4) Celebrity problem.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "H1yKfiw5cF_Wfb3PgvE1y",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1009.0715975080197,
      "y": 10785.710597507528,
      "width": 1422.89892578125,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 957101046,
      "version": 2151,
      "versionNonce": 1653278058,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1782923761831,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Load Data in Redis\nTwo ways\n1) First way.\n    1) When user come to book, Check Redis for seat if there is no entry which means either same seat got booked or timer got expired. \n    check DB if seat available then do entry in Redis for the same seat , train id with expire time.\n    2) When other user come to book same seat within train get data from redis. \nproblem:\n    suppose train has 500 seat and at a time 1M user hit same service and found no entry in Redis, so total 500M DB hit and 500 Write hit \nSolution:\n   DB replica : read replica can get 500M hit for check entry and write replica can get 500 write hit \n\n2) Second way.\n   1) When data load or change of train in DB. we load seat plus train id data in to Redis without expire time called (seat mapping).\n   2) Now when user come to book data it will get data from Redis. ( available seat, train Id).\n   3) Specific seat are allocated and change their status with expire time.\n   4) If payment done within time changed status to booked in Redis. if payment failed/time expired change status of those seat to unreserved.\n   5) When all seat got booked. update all data with status into DB.\n problem:\n  1) how to store passenger details. because you are updating data batch wise into DB. Where and how to store all passanger details ? \n\nHere one improvement\n1) In train user are not allowed to do booking of specific seats. So we can do locking on counter can also good.\n \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Load Data in Redis\nTwo ways\n1) First way.\n    1) When user come to book, Check Redis for seat if there is no entry which means either same seat got booked or timer got expired. \n    check DB if seat available then do entry in Redis for the same seat , train id with expire time.\n    2) When other user come to book same seat within train get data from redis. \nproblem:\n    suppose train has 500 seat and at a time 1M user hit same service and found no entry in Redis, so total 500M DB hit and 500 Write hit \nSolution:\n   DB replica : read replica can get 500M hit for check entry and write replica can get 500 write hit \n\n2) Second way.\n   1) When data load or change of train in DB. we load seat plus train id data in to Redis without expire time called (seat mapping).\n   2) Now when user come to book data it will get data from Redis. ( available seat, train Id).\n   3) Specific seat are allocated and change their status with expire time.\n   4) If payment done within time changed status to booked in Redis. if payment failed/time expired change status of those seat to unreserved.\n   5) When all seat got booked. update all data with status into DB.\n problem:\n  1) how to store passenger details. because you are updating data batch wise into DB. Where and how to store all passanger details ? \n\nHere one improvement\n1) In train user are not allowed to do booking of specific seats. So we can do locking on counter can also good.\n \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
